      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T09:26:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, that\u0027s a good observation, this is sketchy as first uploaded. I had assumed that `--in-reply-to` would override the `--path` since the REST API documentation claims the path is optional, but a closer read revealed that it\u0027s actually required for this pattern.\n\nI followed the same pattern as git_cl now, to infer the path from the `in-reply-to` by first loading the comment thread and then populating the reply from that (cf. https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/tools/depot_tools/+/main:git_cl.py;l\u003d5864-5909;drc\u003dce92a2e156beaaf1f2ed3a651a5c96f55bb78b80)\n\nPTAL again.",
